WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.240
Would you pull it together already?

3
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.040
Why do all your moves
suck so much, huh?

4
00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.640
That's one for Ace.

5
00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:58.800
[sighs]
Just give it up
with the rubber crap.

6
00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:06.030
<b>Oath of Brotherhood</b>

7
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.700
Or at least learn to fight
like a normal person first.

8
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.870
No way! I was so close!

9
00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.640
Just you wait, it's gonna be
awesome when I get it right!

10
00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.210
C'mon, one more try!

11
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.250
Sorry, man.

12
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.550
You know the rules...
a hundred matches a day.

13
00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.050
You can try it tomorrow.

14
00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:18.070
[SABO]
Luffy lost 50 times to both of us.

15
00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:21.700
Me versus Ace looks like 24 to 26.

16
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.270
Lost by two points. So close!

17
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.710
You just win 'cause you're older.

18
00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.330
I'm telling you, when I turn
ten, I'm gonna kick your butts!

19
00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.700
You do realize we'll be 13 then, right?

20
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.260
Anyway, let's go look
for something to eat.

21
00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.270
That looks yummy.

22
00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.570
I could eat crocodile every day!

23
00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:49.270
Okay, but make sure he
doesn't eat you this time.

24
00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.910
You're lucky you got
swallowed whole before.

25
00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.710
Better safe than sorry, huh?

26
00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.250
You can't swim, so stay
up here and watch.

27
00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.750
Crocodile meat!

28
00:03:58.750 --> 00:03:59.750
[SABO screams]

29
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.990
If you don't die,
I'm so gonna kill you!

30
00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:15.630
[NARRATOR]
The harsh environment of Mount Corvo made
the three boys grow stronger each day.

31
00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.890
[NARRATOR]
To the north of
their forest playground,

32
00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:24.320
the dirty dealings of Gray
Terminal continued as usual.

33
00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:30.260
[NARRATOR]
And even further north than that,
there was a city with a solid stone wall,

34
00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.830
handily keeping the nearby
criminals at arm's length.

35
00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.940
[NARRATOR]
The only entrance from the junkyard
below is called the Great Gate.

36
00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.570
Twice a day, mountains
of discarded trash

37
00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:49.800
from all over the country are carried
through it and dumped into Gray Terminal.

38
00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.710
- [SCAVENGERS chuckle]
- Here it comes.

39
00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.310
Let's go! Treasure huntin' time!

40
00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.780
[NARRATOR]
From time to time,
residents of Gray Terminal

41
00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.950
will enter the city to sell
what they call "recycled goods."

42
00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.420
[GUARD A]
Huh? Hey, wait!

43
00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.090
What's in that package?

44
00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.010
Crocodile skin. Want it?

45
00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.180
[GUARD A]
What?

46
00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.950
[GUARD A gasps]
G-Go ahead!

47
00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.620
[NARRATOR]
Beyond the Great Gate is a boulevard,

48
00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:27.020
through which everyone
entering the city must pass.

49
00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.680
It leads to Edge Town.

50
00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:37.030
[NARRATOR]
Edge Town, populated
by thugs and criminals,

51
00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:40.500
lacks the refinement seen
in the rest of the city.

52
00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.370
Hey there, buddy.

53
00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.600
Need some help with that heavy package?

54
00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.140
[HOODLUMS chuckle]

55
00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:55.140
Hey! Answer me when I speak to you!

56
00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.500
[ACE]
Buzz off.

57
00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.300
What?

58
00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.940
[HOODLUMS gasp]

59
00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.540
You're dead!

60
00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.140
Gotta pick your targets more carefully!

61
00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.960
You might get more than
you bargained for.

62
00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.330
[HOODLUMS gasp]

63
00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:13.500
Aw, damn it, not them! Look out!

64
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:14.670
[ACE]
No mercy!

65
00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.370
[SABO, LUFFY]
– All right!
– All right!

66
00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.110
- [thudding]
- [HOODLUMS groaning]

67
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.980
[CROWD chattering]

68
00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:38.370
[NARRATOR]
In the middle of the city, another
stone wall reaches to the skies.

69
00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.700
This one encloses High Town,
which separates those

70
00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.240
with noble blood from
their "lessor" neighbors.

71
00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.210
[NARRATOR]
This is the shining
jewel of the Goa Kingdom.

72
00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:53.680
Said to be the most beautiful
country in all of the East Blue,

73
00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.850
not a hint of trash can
be found on its streets.

74
00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.660
[NARRATOR]
Windmill Village
can make no such claim.

75
00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:00.800
<b>Edge 
Town</b>

76
00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:05.900
<b>Foosha
Village</b>

77
00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:06.000
<b>High Town</b>
<b>Midtown</b>
<b>Gray 
Terminal</b>

78
00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:06.140
<b>Palace</b>
<b>Mount
 Colubo</b>

79
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:06.000
<b>Edge 
Town Foosha
Village</b>

80
00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:04.490
And although it's technically
a part of the Goa Kingdom,

81
00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.490
the fact is often swept under the rug

82
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.210
<b>Edge 
Town Foosha
Village</b>

83
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.240
<b>High Town</b>
<b>Gray 
Terminal</b>
<b>Foosha
Village</b>

84
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:12.310
<b>Midtown</b>

85
00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:09.240
<b>Palace</b>
<b>Mount
 Colubo</b>

86
00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.360
by its more wealthy inhabitants.

87
00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:09.240
<b>Edge 
Town</b>

88
00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.800
[CROWD chattering]

89
00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:13.880
<b>Fine Dining Eiichiro</b>

90
00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:18.890
[WAITRESS A]
Three bowls of
ramen. Thank you for waiting.

91
00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.390
Enjoy your meal.

92
00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.790
So, this is ramen, huh?

93
00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.290
Whoa, looks good!

94
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.460
Well, eat it already!

95
00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.770
Took the words right outta my mouth!

96
00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.640
Seconds, please...

97
00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.780
Ahem. We require seconds.

98
00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.120
Three more bowls, post haste!

99
00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.850
[WAITRESS A]
Yes, sir! On the way!

100
00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.780
[WAITRESS A]
May I come in?

101
00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.660
[screams]

102
00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:58.920
[WAITRESS A panting]

103
00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.830
[RAMEN MAN A]
Are you sure?

104
00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.930
Sir, I think we need to talk.

105
00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.160
[SABO, ACE, LUFFY gasp]

106
00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:07.360
[ACE]
They found us out!

107
00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.170
[SABO]
Yeah! Book it!

108
00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.130
[RAMEN MAN A]
It's a dine and dash!

109
00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.990
Catch those criminals!

110
00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.830
Ahh. Wow, ramen sure is good!

111
00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.230
[ACE]
I know, right? Worth it!

112
00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.260
[LUFFY]
Mm-hmm!

113
00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.230
[MAN E]
"Criminals"?

114
00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.400
[MAN F]
They're just kids!

115
00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.900
[CROWD gasps]

116
00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.100
Damn it, how did those little
pests sneak through the gate again?

117
00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.560
I've had enough of their
antics for a lifetime!

118
00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.010
Don't let them get away!

119
00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:35.010
I don't care if they're kids!
They belong in a damn jail!

120
00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.630
[WAITRESS A]
Did they realize
they were on the fourth floor?

121
00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.970
Because that is a long fall.

122
00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:43.370
The window is a mess.

123
00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.870
but we lost 26 bowls of ramen, too!

124
00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.200
Sir, look at this.

125
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.210
Those kids left a weird note.

126
00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.050
[RAMEN MAN A gasps]

127
00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:58.350
<b>PUT IT ON MY 
TREASURE TAB 
- LUFFY</b>

128
00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:57.020
[RAMEN MAN A]
What is a "treasure tab"?

129
00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.520
Huh? Wait, Sabo?

130
00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.730
I can't believe it's him!

131
00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.060
Please, come back!

132
00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.300
It's you! You're alive!

133
00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.690
[SABO'S DAD]
Let's go home!

134
00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:13.760
The hell is this?

135
00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.600
Are you friends with
that old dude, Sabo?

136
00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.600
I think he knows you.

137
00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.330
He's confusing me with
someone else, that's all.

138
00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.010
[gasps]
No! Sabo, come back!

139
00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.060
Sabo.

140
00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.760
[DADAN]
"We will have a visit this spring."

141
00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.860
Dogra! Magra!

142
00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.930
What is Goa? A country?

143
00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.760
[DOGRA]
Uh, that's the country we live in.

144
00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:53.140
Mount Corvo, Windmill Village,
and Gray Terminal are all part of Goa.

145
00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.640
[DADAN]
Hmph. I knew that.

146
00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.770
It must be the end of the world.

147
00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:00.210
I wasn't even sure you could read
and now you're reading the paper?

148
00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.170
Frankly, it's kinda creeping me out.

149
00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:04.130
- [thud]
- [MAGRA] Ow!

150
00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.030
[DADAN]
Anyway, they're making
a big deal about this visit,

151
00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:11.170
but it's not like they're gonna haul
their asses all the way to our mountain.

152
00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:15.040
Not that I'd want to see
those pompous bastards anyway.

153
00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.910
Celestial Dragons?

154
00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:21.030
<b>A CELESTIAL DRAGON WILL VISIT</b>

155
00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:18.260
No thanks.

156
00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:31.390
You're wrong! I'm not hiding anything!

157
00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.090
[LUFFY]
Oh, that's cool, then.

158
00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.460
Come on, how stupid can you get?

159
00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.230
He's full of it!

160
00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.930
Dammit, Sabo, we can't keep
secrets from each other!

161
00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:45.940
[BOTH]
– So, talk!
– So, talk!

162
00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:52.110
There's nothing for me to tell you.

163
00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:55.680
You trying to pick a fight
with me? Spit it out already!

164
00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.450
[SABO]
Okay, okay, just stop killing me!

165
00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:03.120
[LUFFY]
Huh?!

166
00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.960
[ACE]
The son of a noble?

167
00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:07.860
[ACE, LUFFY]
– Who is?
– Who is?

168
00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.290
I am!

169
00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.360
[BOTH]
– Hmm. So?
– Hmm. So?

170
00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:15.200
If you don't care,
then why did you ask me?

171
00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:21.270
[SABO]
The truth is, both my
parents are still alive.

172
00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:23.440
So yeah, I'm not an orphan.

173
00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:26.880
That means I lied about growing
up in Gray Terminal, too.

174
00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:29.950
And that guy who was
calling out to me...

175
00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:31.910
[SABO]
That was my dad.

176
00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.880
[gasps]

177
00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.140
[SABO]
I'm sorry.

178
00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:38.580
I know I've been lying to you
guys for a long time now.

179
00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:41.180
Well, he said he's sorry,
so we gotta forgive him.

180
00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:44.750
I'm not forgiving anyone
till I hear the whole story.

181
00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.860
If you're really from a noble family,

182
00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.690
why would you want to live
in some crappy junk heap?

183
00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.920
'Cause I ran away
from home, that's why.

184
00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.380
[ACE, LUFFY gasp]

185
00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.160
[SABO'S DAD]
You understand, don't you, Sabo?

186
00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:08.170
[SABO'S DAD]
A noble must be a gentleman,
educated, well-mannered, and wise.

187
00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:12.100
And then, when you're older, you can
marry a girl from a royal family.

188
00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:14.770
That will make Mommy
and Daddy very happy.

189
00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:17.600
Of course, I'm sure
you'll be very happy, too.

190
00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.920
Hello? Hello?

191
00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:23.760
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL A]
Cah-lick.

192
00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.820
[SABO'S DAD groans]

193
00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.690
I cannot afford this.

194
00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.160
What a mess.

195
00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.490
[knocking]

196
00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.100
Hey, Dad! Look at this!

197
00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.700
<b>DAD</b>

198
00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.830
I drew it for you!

199
00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:41.880
[gasps]

200
00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:44.340
Your father is having
a trying day at work.

201
00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:48.950
Sabo, if you have time to draw
this, you have time to study.

202
00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:52.650
<b>DAD</b>

203
00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.590
[NOBLE BOY A]
Hey, you!

204
00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:01.960
[SABO]
Uh...

205
00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.030
[NOBLE BOY A]
I'm from the royal family!

206
00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.770
And that means you have
to do everything I say!

207
00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.170
Carry me back to my house.

208
00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.440
[NOBLE BOY A gasps]
How dare you!

209
00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.010
I'm related to the king and I
want a piggyback ride right now!

210
00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.480
Stop! Get offa me!

211
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.300
You nobles think you're
so hot, don't you?

212
00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.800
This oughta teach you!

213
00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:35.700
[gasps]

214
00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.340
[SABO]
No!

215
00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:43.320
[crying]

216
00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:47.660
My son has royal blood... I won't stand for
you spilling it on the pavement, you oaf!

217
00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.370
[SABO'S MOM gsps]
Sabo, tell me you didn't get in a fight

218
00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.580
with this boy from the royal family!

219
00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.810
Well, kind of.

220
00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.920
I mean, he attacked me
with this scary knife, so...

221
00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.350
[SABO'S MOM grunts]

222
00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:06.250
My son can be such a little beast!

223
00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:09.050
I blame myself...
I do hope you weren't hurt!

224
00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.420
It's terrible, I know.

225
00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:11.590
Please forgive us.

226
00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:14.020
I assure you, he will be
punished severely for this.

227
00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:16.190
I'll do anything I can
to make things right.

228
00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:19.630
Shall we go to the doctor to make
sure your son isn't injured?

229
00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:24.870
[SABO]
Then I realized,
they love their money...

230
00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.940
their property... their status...

231
00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:30.950
[SABO]
...but not their son.

232
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:37.610
[SABO]
If I couldn't marry into a royal
family, I was useless to them.

233
00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:41.410
They tried to teach me culture and
literature and all that stuff...

234
00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:43.280
but I guess I didn't
learn fast enough,

235
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:46.240
'cause they were always
arguing and getting mad.

236
00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:49.610
That family had no place
for someone like me.

237
00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:54.690
I know you guys have it worse, but even
if I had parents, I was still alone.

238
00:14:55.720 --> 00:15:00.920
[SABO'S DAD]
I heard that you've been sneaking out
behind my back going goodness knows where.

239
00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.530
I shouldn't have to tell you this,

240
00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:07.000
but stay away from Gray Terminal
if you know what's good for you.

241
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.530
We nobles are privileged to live in
High Town with the king and his family.

242
00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:13.770
It's a life the people down
there can only dream of.

243
00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:17.940
By the same token, you do not
belong in their world.

244
00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:23.900
Well, at least the people in Gray
Terminal know what it means to be free.

245
00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.310
If the nobles in High Town
didn't spend their whole lives

246
00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.070
licking the boots of the royal family,

247
00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:31.080
maybe they'd look up and see
that there's more to the world.

248
00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:34.820
Man, I had no idea.

249
00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:37.490
[SABO]
Ace, Luffy, listen.

250
00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.000
The three of us,
we're gonna leave this country.

251
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.100
We're gonna sail the seas
and see the world.

252
00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:48.590
And once I've done it all,
I'm gonna write a book for kids like me.

253
00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.960
'Cause studying is fun when
you're learning about adventure!

254
00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.760
And we're gonna have lots of 'em.

255
00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.960
We're gonna be pirates!

256
00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:59.900
[BOTH chuckle]

257
00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:02.300
[ACE]
You don't gotta tell me!

258
00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:04.100
I'm gonna be a pirate anyway!

259
00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.900
I'll be so tough that all the other pirates
and all the Marines will bow at my feet.

260
00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.600
Everyone in the world
will know my name!

261
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:14.100
That's gonna be the legacy
I leave behind when I die!

262
00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.800
I don't care if people hate me.

263
00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.210
I don't care if they wish
I'd never been born.

264
00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.710
But they won't ignore me.

265
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.380
That's what it means to be strong!

266
00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.280
To be a great pirate!

267
00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.950
I won't ever lose and
I won't ever run away!

268
00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:30.490
Who cares if the world fears me
or respects me or whatever.

269
00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:33.170
I'm gonna be a legend!

270
00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:34.470
[chuckles]

271
00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.910
[LUFFY]
Then I know what I'm gonna be, too!

272
00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:43.820
The king of the pirates!

273
00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:46.970
[BOTH gasp]

274
00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:50.140
[laughing]

275
00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.250
You dork.

276
00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.830
Just gotta try and
show me up, don'tcha?

277
00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:56.330
[SABO laughs]

278
00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.940
I dunno if you'll be a king or not,
but you're gonna do something crazy,

279
00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:02.210
I know that much for sure!

280
00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:05.540
Uh... We all wanna be pirates
together, though, don't we?

281
00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:10.280
We're only saving for one ship, but what
if all three of us wanna be captain?

282
00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:12.250
Damn it, I never thought of that.

283
00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:15.920
Sabo, I always figured you'd
be the navigator on my ship.

284
00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:18.190
You guys are welcome to join my crew!

285
00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.320
[ACE, SABO]
– No thanks!
– No thanks!

286
00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.750
[ACE]
Well, we'll figure it
out when the time comes.

287
00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.920
Maybe we'll leave on one ship
and maybe we'll leave on three.

288
00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.720
[LUFFY]
Ooh! You stole that from Dadan, huh?

289
00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.990
Lemme tell you guys a secret.

290
00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:40.630
[ACE]
All it takes to become
brothers is to share some saké!

291
00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:43.330
Whoa, really? That's so cool!

292
00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:47.740
[ACE]
We may sail in different seas, with
different crews on different ships.

293
00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:51.180
But wherever we go and
whatever adventures we have,

294
00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:55.480
we'll always be brothers,
and nobody can take that away.

295
00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:56.610
[giggles]

296
00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:57.780
[ACE]
Heh.

297
00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.980
From now on, we're honest
to goodness brothers.

298
00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.590
Cheers to that!

299
00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:11.150
[ALL]
– Brothers!
– Brothers!

300
00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.070
<b>We're going independent.</b>

301
00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.470
Give him back, ya jerk!

302
00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.970
What do you mean "give
him back," you filthy rat?

303
00:19:57.970 --> 00:19:59.440
Sabo is my son!

304
00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:04.180
Which means that he's obligated to live
on the path that I have prepared for him!

305
00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.980
You should be ashamed, steering him
toward the life of a petty thief!

306
00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:10.770
You're both nothing but wannabe thugs!

307
00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.770
Why did you do it? For my money?

308
00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:15.360
Screw your damn money!

309
00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.260
[ACE groans]

310
00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.360
Ack. You foolish pirate!

311
00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:20.950
Quit knocking that kid
around so carelessly!

312
00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:24.160
You'll get that delinquent's
disgusting blood on my nice clothes!

313
00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:25.160
[ACE growls]

314
00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:25.920
Hey, Ace!

315
00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:26.890
[SABO grunts]

316
00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.860
[BLUEJAM PIRATE H]
Hey, come back here!

317
00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:30.060
[SABO]
Stop this, okay?

318
00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.630
Nobody tempted me to do anything!

319
00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:34.640
I only ran away 'cause I wanted to!

320
00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:37.510
I'll be dealing with
you later, Sabo. Take him!

321
00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:41.480
Deal with the other two
however you see fit.

322
00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:45.410
Not a problem, sir, you've
already paid us quite handsomely.

323
00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.610
We'll make sure these two
never bother your boy again.

324
00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:51.150
I'll spare you the gory details.

325
00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.510
Wait, Bluejam! Please don't hurt them!

326
00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.410
Call them off, Dad,
I get it! Please stop!

327
00:20:57.410 --> 00:21:00.380
Huh? What do you mean, you "get it"?

328
00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.750
I'll do whatever you
want me to do, okay?

329
00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:10.520
I'll live whatever life
you've mapped out.

330
00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:15.160
Just please. I'm begging you,
don't hurt my friends.

331
00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:17.230
They've done nothing wrong.

332
00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:18.830
I can't stand this.

333
00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.230
Those two are my brothers.

334
00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:23.560
Sabo, no.

335
00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:26.810
Oh? If that's what
you want, then go home.

336
00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:31.450
And promise you'll stop playing pirate
with lowlifes in this trash heap.

337
00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.750
No! Don't do it!

338
00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.050
[BLUEJAM PIRATE I]
Shut up, kid!

339
00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:38.560
Dammit, Sabo. Run away from them!

340
00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.830
Luffy and I can take care of ourselves!

341
00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:43.600
This is your life, you have to be free!

342
00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:46.360
He's right! Don't go!

343
00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:49.270
[ACE]
Are you gonna abandon all
your dreams, just like that?

344
00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:50.530
Sabo!

345
00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:55.800
Sabo!

346
00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:56.970
[gasps]

347
00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.360
[ACE]
Sabo!

348
00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.300
Hey, Captain!

349
00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:11.730
What do you want us to do
with the other ones?

350
00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:13.670
We'll take them back to the hideout.

351
00:22:13.670 --> 00:22:15.070
[BLUEJAM PIRATE J]
Yes, sir.

352
00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:24.130
[BLUEJAM]
It must be awful nice to be a noble.

353
00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:26.400
Wouldn't you punks agree?

354
00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:29.570
To them, we're no different than
the piles of garbage we live in.

355
00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:32.370
They just sit back while
we do all the dirty work.

356
00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:35.400
It's a pretty cushy life
your buddy's living, I'd say.

357
00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:37.580
You got no clue what
you're talking about!

358
00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:40.480
Pirate life is way better
than being a stupid noble!

359
00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:41.880
Sabo said so himself!

360
00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:45.180
You kids are so hopeless I
can't help feeling bad for you.

361
00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:46.850
Hey, untie their ropes, and quick.

362
00:22:46.850 --> 00:22:47.880
[BLUEJAM PIRATE K]
Yes, sir.

363
00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:51.890
Why do you think a kid from a noble family
ran off to a place like Gray Terminal?

364
00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:55.130
Did you think he just wanted
to make some new friends?

365
00:22:55.130 --> 00:22:57.860
He was mocking you and
all the other people here,

366
00:22:57.860 --> 00:23:01.600
just like adult nobles do
when they're feeling bored.

367
00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:04.960
Real sorry to break it to you.
That boy's no friend of yours.

368
00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:07.970
You're lying! Sabo would never
pull a stunt like that!

369
00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:10.740
He's right! He said we were
brothers, you heard him!

370
00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:14.270
Yeah, guess so. Whatever
you kids say. Ha, ha, ha.

371
00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:19.040
But in any case, you boys aren't gonna
bother him or his family anymore, are you?

372
00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.540
'Cause if that's the plan,

373
00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.010
I'm afraid I'd have to take you
both out right here and now.

374
00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:25.850
If you really think of
him as your brother,

375
00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:27.980
it'd be best for everyone
to leave him alone.

376
00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:29.110
[gasps]

377
00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:30.580
[ACE]
Leave him alone?

378
00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:32.140
What about our dream?

379
00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:34.480
No! Sabo told us that
he hates High Town!

380
00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:37.040
Look, if you really care
about this Sabo kid,

381
00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:39.670
then you gotta let him
go live his own life.

382
00:23:39.670 --> 00:23:41.590
You'll understand when you grow up.

383
00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:45.110
Anyway, until recently,
I had a bone to pick with you

384
00:23:45.110 --> 00:23:47.660
after what happened with
Porchemy and our money.

385
00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:49.230
But I'm over all that now.

386
00:23:49.230 --> 00:23:52.300
In fact, I'm kind of impressed at
how tough you little punks are.

387
00:23:52.300 --> 00:23:54.730
Which is why I wanted
to ask you something.

388
00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:57.000
It might just be worth your while.

389
00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:59.670
Thanks to you boys,
I'm kinda short-handed.

390
00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:03.210
So, how would you feel
about doing a job for me?

391
00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.680
Don't worry. It's a short, easy gig.

392
00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:08.910
There's actually not really
much danger involved.

393
00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:11.330
On that barrel's a
map of Gray Terminal.

394
00:24:11.330 --> 00:24:15.470
You just have to carry packages to the
locations marked on the map with an "X."

395
00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:17.070
You interested?

396
00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:18.070
Okay, sure.

397
00:24:18.070 --> 00:24:19.410
[LUFFY gasps]

398
00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:21.050
What about pay?

399
00:24:25.410 --> 00:24:27.510
My head is tired.

400
00:24:27.510 --> 00:24:29.490
Hauling stuff is no fun
if Sabo's not around.

401
00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:30.690
Just deal with it.

402
00:24:30.690 --> 00:24:32.090
I don't like this either.

403
00:24:32.090 --> 00:24:34.500
I'd much rather find
Sabo and rescue him.

404
00:24:34.500 --> 00:24:38.370
But Bluejam had a point. We've
gotta let him live his own life.

405
00:24:39.560 --> 00:24:41.000
Look, give it some time.

406
00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.900
He's gonna be all right
and if he doesn't like it,

407
00:24:43.900 --> 00:24:46.480
he can always come and join us again.

408
00:24:46.480 --> 00:24:50.710
Until that happens, let's keep
putting money in the pirate fund.

409
00:24:52.170 --> 00:24:53.240
[SABO]
Believe what you want,

410
00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:54.980
it's still not Ace and Luffy's fault.

411
00:24:54.980 --> 00:24:58.180
[SABO'S DAD]
Quit wasting
our time! Tell us the truth!

412
00:24:58.180 --> 00:24:59.450
Wait just a minute.

413
00:24:59.450 --> 00:25:01.390
Those scoundrels must
have threatened you.

414
00:25:01.390 --> 00:25:03.250
They really have you
wrapped around their fingers.

415
00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:06.210
No! They aren't those
kind of people, okay?

416
00:25:06.210 --> 00:25:08.410
Any noble with a
criminal record to his name

417
00:25:08.410 --> 00:25:11.040
will damage his family's
hard-earned reputation.

418
00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:13.280
You would also be barred
from entering High Town.

419
00:25:13.280 --> 00:25:15.200
Those two forced you to leave home

420
00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:19.600
and get involved with their atrocious acts
of violence against your better judgment.

421
00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:21.640
Isn't that right, Sabo?

422
00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.170
Look here, son. The fate of
your friends in Gray Terminal

423
00:25:27.170 --> 00:25:28.570
is in the hands of pirates.

424
00:25:28.570 --> 00:25:30.510
Those pirates work for me.

425
00:25:30.510 --> 00:25:33.120
All I need to do is give the order.

426
00:25:33.120 --> 00:25:35.550
If these slum brats are that important,

427
00:25:35.550 --> 00:25:38.950
think long and hard about
what you have to do.

428
00:25:41.210 --> 00:25:43.910
[SABO'S DAD]
You're a smart boy,
born to a great family.

429
00:25:43.910 --> 00:25:46.380
You already know what's right.

430
00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:48.010
You promised me you wouldn't hurt them.

431
00:25:48.010 --> 00:25:50.080
That's the only reason
I came back here!

432
00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:52.650
You haven't changed at
all since I ran away!

433
00:25:52.650 --> 00:25:54.180
No one tempted me!

434
00:25:54.180 --> 00:25:57.350
I've made every decision
by my own free will!

435
00:25:57.350 --> 00:25:59.790
[groans]

436
00:25:59.790 --> 00:26:02.360
[SABO'S DAD]
You disappoint me!

437
00:26:02.360 --> 00:26:06.600
I apologize, sir, I'm so ashamed
that I have such a foolish son!

438
00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:09.370
Surely you understand my dilemma?

439
00:26:09.370 --> 00:26:13.670
[COP A]
Of course!
It must tear you apart inside.

440
00:26:13.670 --> 00:26:16.470
Don't you worry, I'll take
care of all the paperwork.

441
00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:18.840
[SABO groans]

442
00:26:19.300 --> 00:26:21.050
[SERVANT A]
Welcome back, sir.

443
00:26:22.230 --> 00:26:24.670
Home at last. Let's go, Sabo.

444
00:26:24.670 --> 00:26:26.540
You've been gone quite some time.

445
00:26:26.540 --> 00:26:30.740
Ah! On second thought, don't
come in yet. You must be filthy.

446
00:26:30.740 --> 00:26:35.110
Hose yourself off in the yard first,
then come in and take a bath.

447
00:26:35.110 --> 00:26:38.380
[SERVANT A]
We're all glad that you're
back home safe, young master.

448
00:26:38.380 --> 00:26:41.150
Oh, goodness! Is it really you?

449
00:26:41.150 --> 00:26:43.980
You've grown so big! [laughs]

450
00:26:43.980 --> 00:26:45.150
Hello, Mom.

451
00:26:45.150 --> 00:26:48.050
Now, Stelly, say hello
to your brother Sabo.

452
00:26:48.050 --> 00:26:50.550
Nice to meet you, big brother!

453
00:26:50.550 --> 00:26:53.810
I'm Stelly and I'm
eight! What about you?

454
00:26:53.810 --> 00:26:55.250
[SABO]
What the hell?

455
00:26:56.380 --> 00:26:57.650
We adopted him.

456
00:26:57.650 --> 00:27:00.210
He's a promising boy
from another noble family.

457
00:27:00.210 --> 00:27:04.850
For reasons beyond understanding,
his parents suddenly became neglectful.

458
00:27:04.850 --> 00:27:07.910
So far he's fit in extremely well.

459
00:27:07.910 --> 00:27:09.980
I imagine that if things
don't work out with you

460
00:27:09.980 --> 00:27:13.050
when it's time to choose a
successor, then he would...

461
00:27:13.050 --> 00:27:15.300
Ugh, no, no, never mind.

462
00:27:15.300 --> 00:27:16.530
I've said too much.

463
00:27:16.530 --> 00:27:18.200
Go and get settled in your room.

464
00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:20.840
You'll resume your
studies tomorrow morning.

465
00:27:30.010 --> 00:27:32.610
[ACE]
Are you gonna abandon all
your dreams, just like that?

466
00:27:32.610 --> 00:27:34.140
[knocking]

467
00:27:35.770 --> 00:27:37.900
Hey! Do you know what I heard?

468
00:27:37.900 --> 00:27:40.940
You're as dumb as a brick. [chuckles]

469
00:27:40.940 --> 00:27:45.010
That's what Mama and Papa think,
in case you couldn't guess.

470
00:27:45.010 --> 00:27:47.270
But still, you sure are lucky.

471
00:27:47.270 --> 00:27:50.740
Tomorrow night they're
taking care of the garbage.

472
00:27:50.740 --> 00:27:55.050
To think, had you stayed in
Gray Terminal a day longer,

473
00:27:55.050 --> 00:27:57.690
you'd be dead like
the rest of the crooks.

474
00:27:58.690 --> 00:27:59.890
Too bad.

475
00:27:59.890 --> 00:28:02.290
My life would be a lot easier
if you never came back,

476
00:28:02.290 --> 00:28:04.490
but I'm clever enough, so I'll make do.

477
00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:07.090
[gasps]
Hey, ow! Stop!

478
00:28:07.090 --> 00:28:08.950
Let go of me or I'll tell Papa!

479
00:28:08.950 --> 00:28:11.780
What did you say? What's going on?

480
00:28:11.780 --> 00:28:14.250
You tell me everything,
or I'll beat you up!

481
00:28:14.250 --> 00:28:17.790
Wait! Tomorrow?
There's going to be a fire.

482
00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:19.420
They're burning Gray Terminal.

483
00:28:19.420 --> 00:28:20.190
A fire?

484
00:28:20.190 --> 00:28:21.520
That's right.

485
00:28:21.520 --> 00:28:24.810
You didn't hear about it because
you've been away for so long.

486
00:28:24.810 --> 00:28:27.680
The nobles in High Town
decided it months ago.

487
00:28:27.680 --> 00:28:33.270
The World Government is sending a group
of people to check out all of the East Blue.

488
00:28:33.270 --> 00:28:37.270
They're finally gonna arrive in
Goa Kingdom three days from now!

489
00:28:37.270 --> 00:28:42.550
Rumor has it they have a World Noble,
a Celestial Dragon with them.

490
00:28:42.550 --> 00:28:44.120
People are panicking!

491
00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:46.150
The members of the royal
family don't want him

492
00:28:46.150 --> 00:28:48.660
to see all the dirty
parts of this country.

493
00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:52.560
So they made the obvious decision
to burn down Gray Terminal!

494
00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:56.250
It's a surefire way to cleanse
this country of all its rubbish!

495
00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:59.270
There's no way they'd just burn
everything down without warning!

496
00:28:59.270 --> 00:29:01.370
Don't joke about something like that!

497
00:29:01.370 --> 00:29:03.910
There's a lot of people
living in Gray Terminal!

498
00:29:03.910 --> 00:29:07.120
They can't just torch down their
homes because they feel like it!

499
00:29:07.120 --> 00:29:08.510
Get off of me!

500
00:29:08.510 --> 00:29:09.850
You really are stupid.

501
00:29:09.850 --> 00:29:13.220
Haven't you heard a
single thing I've said?

502
00:29:13.220 --> 00:29:15.090
All the shame of this country.

503
00:29:15.090 --> 00:29:17.820
Tomorrow they're gonna
burn it all away.

504
00:29:17.820 --> 00:29:20.730
The people, too?

505
00:29:26.930 --> 00:29:28.800
Hey. Wait up!

506
00:29:30.470 --> 00:29:32.040
Where are you going?

507
00:29:36.070 --> 00:29:39.470
[gasps]
You can't jump
out the window like that!

508
00:29:41.890 --> 00:29:44.680
Wow. He's a goner.

509
00:29:44.680 --> 00:29:46.840
[SABO]
It's a lie. It's gotta be!

510
00:29:46.840 --> 00:29:49.040
They can't burn down a place that big!

511
00:29:49.040 --> 00:29:51.880
And someone would've heard!

512
00:29:51.880 --> 00:29:53.540
[gasps]

513
00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:57.970
[SABO]
Soldiers from this afternoon.

514
00:29:59.060 --> 00:30:00.990
[NOBLE SOLDIER A]
Are we sure we're ready for tomorrow?

515
00:30:00.990 --> 00:30:03.090
There can't be any miscalculations.

516
00:30:03.090 --> 00:30:04.530
[NOBLE SOLDIER B]
We're ready on our end.

517
00:30:04.530 --> 00:30:06.450
But we're stuck relying on the pirates.

518
00:30:06.450 --> 00:30:10.340
They have to burn the trash
precisely at the right time.

519
00:30:10.340 --> 00:30:14.720
[NOBLE SOLDIER A]
Don't worry. Bluejam and his men have
been placing boxes of oil and explosives

520
00:30:14.720 --> 00:30:17.520
all over Gray Terminal,
just like we asked.

521
00:30:19.030 --> 00:30:20.840
[SABO]
Bluejam has a hand in this?

522
00:30:20.840 --> 00:30:22.180
It must be true!

523
00:30:22.180 --> 00:30:24.610
But why? What's in it for him?

524
00:30:35.270 --> 00:30:38.070
Hey, Ace. What d'you
think Sabo's doing?

525
00:30:38.070 --> 00:30:41.370
Seriously? Shut up.

526
00:30:41.370 --> 00:30:44.810
I thought we had agreed to stop
worrying about him for now.

527
00:30:44.810 --> 00:30:46.480
Okay.

528
00:30:46.480 --> 00:30:47.880
Who knows.

529
00:30:47.880 --> 00:30:49.950
This could actually
work out better for him.

530
00:30:53.180 --> 00:30:54.520
[SABO]
Okay, think.

531
00:30:54.520 --> 00:30:57.050
if there was really
gonna be a fire tonight,

532
00:30:57.050 --> 00:30:59.850
the people in the town would
be upset about it, right?

533
00:31:03.560 --> 00:31:05.160
[NOBLE A]
Why, good morning!

534
00:31:05.160 --> 00:31:06.870
A good morning to you, sir!

535
00:31:06.870 --> 00:31:08.570
[NOBLE A]
What a beautiful sunny day!

536
00:31:08.570 --> 00:31:10.040
[NOBLE F]
Yes, lovely.

537
00:31:10.040 --> 00:31:11.270
What a relief!

538
00:31:11.270 --> 00:31:14.170
Guess there's nothing fishy
happening today after all!

539
00:31:14.170 --> 00:31:15.960
I'll walk around for a bit.

540
00:31:18.760 --> 00:31:20.960
[KING A]
Today is windy.

541
00:31:20.960 --> 00:31:23.830
That's true, Your Majesty,
very windy indeed.

542
00:31:23.830 --> 00:31:29.690
[KING A]
Accidents can happen easily on a day
like this, especially wildfires.

543
00:31:29.690 --> 00:31:33.360
How right you are, Majesty.
It's quite possible.

544
00:31:33.360 --> 00:31:36.310
[SABO'S DAD]
What? Sabo snuck out of the house?

545
00:31:36.310 --> 00:31:38.220
He's such an ungrateful brat!

546
00:31:38.220 --> 00:31:40.650
All he cares about is playing
pirate with his friends

547
00:31:40.650 --> 00:31:42.960
when he should stay at home and study!

548
00:31:42.960 --> 00:31:45.460
Have the police search the entire town!

549
00:31:45.460 --> 00:31:49.320
He couldn't have gotten
very far by himself!

550
00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:51.030
Um, excuse me.

551
00:31:51.030 --> 00:31:52.660
What do you want, kid?

552
00:31:52.660 --> 00:31:56.500
[SABO]
Did you know that there's supposed
to be a fire in Gray Terminal tonight?

553
00:31:56.500 --> 00:31:58.570
Of course I know about the fire.

554
00:31:58.570 --> 00:32:01.060
Why, what's wrong, did they cancel it?

555
00:32:01.060 --> 00:32:02.360
[SABO]
He knows.

556
00:32:02.360 --> 00:32:05.260
Tell me, boy,
whose family are you from?

557
00:32:05.260 --> 00:32:07.900
[SABO]
So, it's true!

558
00:32:09.190 --> 00:32:10.090
Hold on!

559
00:32:10.090 --> 00:32:11.790
[SABO]
Everyone knows, don't they?

560
00:32:11.790 --> 00:32:13.560
They have from the start.

561
00:32:13.560 --> 00:32:15.560
Look at them! They're smiling!

562
00:32:15.560 --> 00:32:18.300
They don't give a damn about
the people in Gray Terminal.

563
00:32:18.300 --> 00:32:21.040
They're happy to see them
burn them to the ground!

564
00:32:24.440 --> 00:32:27.580
[BLUEJAM]
You know, we've been waiting on you.

565
00:32:27.580 --> 00:32:29.780
Are there any more boxes
you need us to move?

566
00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:32.920
Yeah, and I've got a
bigger job for you later on,

567
00:32:32.920 --> 00:32:34.970
but we'll talk more about that tonight.

568
00:32:34.970 --> 00:32:37.080
Yes, I heard all about the fire.

569
00:32:37.080 --> 00:32:39.650
And you're not worried? At all?

570
00:32:39.650 --> 00:32:41.980
Nobody in this town cares what happens?

571
00:32:41.980 --> 00:32:45.020
Nobody in town even thinks
of stopping this thing?

572
00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:48.320
That's admirable of you.

573
00:32:48.320 --> 00:32:50.840
You must have a very kind heart.

574
00:32:50.840 --> 00:32:53.670
But, boy, please, don't you say a word.

575
00:32:53.670 --> 00:32:56.770
It's important that we all
keep our mouths shut.

576
00:32:56.770 --> 00:33:02.100
Think. What would happen if someone outside
of High Town found out about the plan?

577
00:33:02.100 --> 00:33:03.830
You and I are special!

578
00:33:03.830 --> 00:33:06.000
We come from great noble families.

579
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:07.240
[SABO screams]

580
00:33:07.240 --> 00:33:09.300
[NOBLE C]
Calm down!

581
00:33:09.300 --> 00:33:11.040
[SABO]
Ace! Luffy!

582
00:33:11.040 --> 00:33:12.970
There's something wrong with this town!

583
00:33:12.970 --> 00:33:15.100
Something wrong with these people!

584
00:33:15.100 --> 00:33:17.050
They know people are gonna die.

585
00:33:17.050 --> 00:33:18.910
They're happy people are going to die!

586
00:33:18.910 --> 00:33:21.550
They're sick! This whole place is sick!

587
00:33:21.550 --> 00:33:23.280
I can't stay here any longer!

588
00:33:23.280 --> 00:33:25.750
I have to tell them, right now!

589
00:33:28.280 --> 00:33:31.280
[SABO]
Today of all days. Why is it so windy?

590
00:33:31.280 --> 00:33:33.450
That's him! That's the missing boy!

591
00:33:33.450 --> 00:33:36.260
Excuse me, kid.
You need to come with us.

592
00:33:36.260 --> 00:33:37.090
[NOBLES gasp]

593
00:33:37.090 --> 00:33:38.990
Hey, you! Stop running!

594
00:33:38.990 --> 00:33:41.460
[SABO]
The nobles here
don't care who they kill.

595
00:33:41.460 --> 00:33:44.760
They'll burn a whole town alive
just 'cause they don't like it!

596
00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:48.700
You gotta get out of Gray Terminal
and you gotta get out now!

597
00:33:48.700 --> 00:33:53.380
Hold on, Ace! Luffy! I'm coming!

598
00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:56.210
But why the hell would
you wanna do that?

599
00:33:56.210 --> 00:33:57.440
[BLUEJAM]
Not so loud!

600
00:33:57.440 --> 00:33:59.410
We gotta keep quiet about this.

601
00:33:59.410 --> 00:34:01.510
If anyone finds out, it won't work.

602
00:34:01.510 --> 00:34:04.510
You really are a meanie, I knew
we shouldn't have trusted you!

603
00:34:04.510 --> 00:34:06.410
We gotta hurry and tell
everyone we can, Ace!

604
00:34:06.410 --> 00:34:08.450
I told you to keep quiet.

605
00:34:08.450 --> 00:34:09.920
Hey. Shut 'em up.

606
00:34:09.920 --> 00:34:11.380
[LUFFY, ACE grunting]

607
00:34:11.380 --> 00:34:13.950
[BLUEJAM]
I'm just following orders, same as you.

608
00:34:13.950 --> 00:34:15.390
[ACE gasps]

609
00:34:15.390 --> 00:34:18.810
[BLUEJAM]
In case you didn't guess, all those
boxes you've been lugging around

610
00:34:18.810 --> 00:34:21.420
are filled with explosives.

611
00:34:21.420 --> 00:34:23.060
You get it?

612
00:34:23.060 --> 00:34:26.290
Nothing will survive
that fire and no one.

613
00:34:26.290 --> 00:34:27.390
[LUFFY gasps]
But...

614
00:34:27.390 --> 00:34:28.890
Bluejam, don't do it!

615
00:34:29.980 --> 00:34:31.630
[laughs]
Since when did you brats

616
00:34:31.630 --> 00:34:34.400
start giving a damn about other people?

617
00:34:34.400 --> 00:34:37.840
Well, now that you know
about the grand plan,

618
00:34:37.840 --> 00:34:40.610
you're stuck here.
We can't risk letting you go.

619
00:34:40.610 --> 00:34:42.210
Sorry.

620
00:34:42.210 --> 00:34:45.810
Actually, there's something I've
been meaning to ask you boys.

621
00:34:45.810 --> 00:34:48.680
Heh. So, tell me.

622
00:34:48.680 --> 00:34:52.720
Is it true that you brats are hiding
treasure somewhere around here?

623
00:34:52.720 --> 00:34:55.290
[LUFFY, ACE grunting]

624
00:35:16.490 --> 00:35:20.160
<b>Edge Town</b>

625
00:35:21.260 --> 00:35:23.490
Stupid dog! Huh?

626
00:35:23.490 --> 00:35:25.660
Hey, wait. What's that?

627
00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:27.130
[MAN B, MAN C]
– Huh?
– Huh?

628
00:35:30.300 --> 00:35:33.140
Something weird is
happening in Gray Terminal.

629
00:35:33.140 --> 00:35:34.600
That looks like fire.

630
00:35:37.940 --> 00:35:42.170
[MAN R laughs]
Who knew the plan
would turn out to be this fun?

631
00:35:42.170 --> 00:35:43.300
[DOGRA]
Hey, boss!

632
00:35:43.300 --> 00:35:46.180
Come quick! Ya gotta see this!

633
00:35:46.180 --> 00:35:47.910
All right, what's the big deal?

634
00:35:47.910 --> 00:35:50.110
It's the sky! Look!

635
00:35:50.110 --> 00:35:51.250
Is that the town?

636
00:35:51.250 --> 00:35:53.080
[BANDIT C]
No, it's closer than that!

637
00:35:53.080 --> 00:35:54.380
I think it's Gray Terminal!

638
00:35:54.380 --> 00:35:55.320
It's on fire!

639
00:35:55.350 --> 00:35:57.490
[DADAN gasps]

640
00:35:57.130 --> 00:35:59.900
<b>Midtown</b>

641
00:35:57.490 --> 00:35:58.610
[MAN S]
What's going on?

642
00:35:58.610 --> 00:36:00.450
Where's that smoke coming from?

643
00:36:00.450 --> 00:36:02.850
[WOMAN A]
Gray Terminal
has never caught fire before.

644
00:36:02.850 --> 00:36:04.150
What happened?

645
00:36:05.320 --> 00:36:06.390
[NOBLE SOLDIER A]
Edge Town is too dangerous,

646
00:36:06.390 --> 00:36:07.920
evacuate immediately!

647
00:36:07.740 --> 00:36:10.380
<b>Edge Town - Great Gate</b>

648
00:36:07.920 --> 00:36:10.930
[NOBLE SOLDIER B]
All residents, please head downtown!

649
00:36:10.930 --> 00:36:13.030
[NOBLE SOLDIER C]
Stay here, where it's safe.

650
00:36:13.030 --> 00:36:15.460
We'll take care of the fire
and other citizens!

651
00:36:15.460 --> 00:36:17.170
[MEN panting]

652
00:36:18.980 --> 00:36:20.310
Everybody, get up!

653
00:36:20.310 --> 00:36:21.480
We gotta escape!

654
00:36:21.480 --> 00:36:22.950
[MAN J gasps]

655
00:36:24.720 --> 00:36:26.950
The fire almost has us surrounded!

656
00:36:26.950 --> 00:36:28.880
Where did this mess even come from?

657
00:36:28.880 --> 00:36:30.250
Look, it's no use, man!

658
00:36:30.250 --> 00:36:31.880
Leave it behind and make a run for it!

659
00:36:31.880 --> 00:36:35.250
[BOTH panting]

660
00:36:35.250 --> 00:36:38.220
[MAN N]
Crap! The fire's
already gotten to the shore!

661
00:36:38.220 --> 00:36:40.430
[MAN O]
The entrance
to the forest is burning, too!

662
00:36:40.430 --> 00:36:43.900
[screams]
We're all gonna
die! Where do we go?

663
00:36:43.900 --> 00:36:47.500
[BLUEJAM PIRATES laughing]

664
00:36:47.500 --> 00:36:49.910
[BLUEJAM]
Say so long to this dump, fellas!

665
00:36:49.910 --> 00:36:52.580
Good riddance! [laughs]

666
00:36:52.580 --> 00:36:55.580
It'll be easy living from here on out!

667
00:36:55.580 --> 00:36:58.920
Yeah, just like the nobles. Heh.

668
00:36:59.790 --> 00:37:00.920
'Course not.

669
00:37:00.920 --> 00:37:05.220
We couldn't care less about the living
garbage stinking up Gray Terminal,

670
00:37:05.220 --> 00:37:07.630
but it makes a good hideout.

671
00:37:07.630 --> 00:37:11.400
The place is huge, plus no
law around to bug us, get it?

672
00:37:11.400 --> 00:37:15.960
[KING]
I'm aware of that, but think,
if you do this for me,

673
00:37:15.960 --> 00:37:18.750
well, you won't need a hideout.

674
00:37:18.750 --> 00:37:23.150
I have the authority to make you
and your crew bona fide nobles.

675
00:37:23.150 --> 00:37:24.820
[ALL gasp]

676
00:37:24.820 --> 00:37:27.820
Really? You'd do that for us?

677
00:37:27.820 --> 00:37:31.320
[BLUEJAM]
Once this is through, the king
of Goa will give us titles!

678
00:37:31.320 --> 00:37:33.990
We'll live in High Town as nobles!

679
00:37:33.990 --> 00:37:35.800
No more of this trash heap!

680
00:37:35.800 --> 00:37:40.370
[laughing]

681
00:37:42.430 --> 00:37:43.830
Now, let's move.

682
00:37:43.830 --> 00:37:46.730
We're almost done and don't worry.

683
00:37:46.730 --> 00:37:49.840
On to the Great Gate!
The military is waiting for us!

684
00:37:49.840 --> 00:37:52.710
[BLUEJAM PIRATE E]
Captain, we left those
two brats in the hideout.

685
00:37:52.710 --> 00:37:53.740
[BLUEJAM]
Forget 'em.

686
00:37:53.740 --> 00:37:55.290
They had their chance to join up

687
00:37:55.290 --> 00:37:58.590
when I asked them where their
treasure was, but they blew it.

688
00:38:00.040 --> 00:38:02.710
[BLUEJAM]
Fools like them
aren't gonna live long, anyway.

689
00:38:02.710 --> 00:38:05.630
[ACE grunting]

690
00:38:05.630 --> 00:38:06.560
[BLUEJAM PIRATE F]
Captain!

691
00:38:06.560 --> 00:38:08.160
The gate is already closed!

692
00:38:08.160 --> 00:38:09.360
[BLUEJAM]
It's nothing.

693
00:38:09.360 --> 00:38:12.140
They just don't want other people
to break in and cause a riot.

694
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:16.040
I'm supposed to give them a sign once
we're here, then they'll open it up.

695
00:38:17.100 --> 00:38:19.870
It's me, Bluejam. We're here.

696
00:38:22.430 --> 00:38:23.530
Huh?

697
00:38:23.530 --> 00:38:26.230
Hey! Open the damn gate!

698
00:38:28.900 --> 00:38:29.940
Captain?

699
00:38:31.170 --> 00:38:33.710
You don't... think...

700
00:38:34.730 --> 00:38:36.000
Hey! Come on!

701
00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:37.570
What the hell are you doing?

702
00:38:37.570 --> 00:38:39.870
This isn't funny! Open the gate!

703
00:38:39.870 --> 00:38:41.110
We made a deal!

704
00:38:41.110 --> 00:38:43.810
You're supposed to let us
evacuate from this pit!

705
00:38:43.810 --> 00:38:45.940
Quit screwing around and let us in!

706
00:38:45.940 --> 00:38:47.870
You bunch of bastards!

707
00:38:47.870 --> 00:38:49.630
The king made me a promise!

708
00:38:49.630 --> 00:38:51.970
If we burned down the terminal,
he'd make us nobles!

709
00:38:51.970 --> 00:38:54.070
Don't tell me he...

710
00:38:55.030 --> 00:38:56.690
[gasps]
The king set us up!

711
00:38:56.690 --> 00:38:59.860
That liar! Dammit!

712
00:39:01.460 --> 00:39:02.500
[CITIZEN A]
Did you hear?

713
00:39:02.500 --> 00:39:03.900
They found out who started the fire.

714
00:39:03.900 --> 00:39:07.490
It was some pirate named
Bluejam from Gray Terminal.

715
00:39:07.490 --> 00:39:08.760
[CITIZEN B]
How despicable!

716
00:39:08.760 --> 00:39:11.060
A criminal turning on his own men!

717
00:39:11.060 --> 00:39:13.900
I bet he was trying to keep the
World Government's observers away

718
00:39:13.900 --> 00:39:15.900
so he could keep on terrorizing people.

719
00:39:15.900 --> 00:39:17.800
Gosh, what an evil pirate!

720
00:39:17.800 --> 00:39:19.300
[ACE panting]

721
00:39:19.300 --> 00:39:21.940
[LUFFY crying]

722
00:39:21.940 --> 00:39:24.870
It's way too hot, Ace!
I think I'm gonna melt!

723
00:39:24.870 --> 00:39:26.220
The hell you are!

724
00:39:26.220 --> 00:39:28.590
Damn! Why did Bluejam
rope us into this mess?

725
00:39:28.590 --> 00:39:32.260
[LUFFY yelling]
We can't get away! I don't wanna die!

726
00:39:32.260 --> 00:39:35.340
If you don't stop complaining,
I'll kill you!

727
00:39:35.340 --> 00:39:36.890
[LUFFY]
It's not that hot.

728
00:39:36.890 --> 00:39:38.190
[ACE, LUFFY panting]

729
00:39:38.190 --> 00:39:40.720
[LUFFY]
Whoa, I'm burning!
I mean this isn't so bad!

730
00:39:40.720 --> 00:39:41.620
[ACE]
It's all over the place!

731
00:39:42.360 --> 00:39:44.360
[coughs]
I can barely breathe.

732
00:39:44.360 --> 00:39:45.860
I mean, I'm cool!

733
00:39:45.860 --> 00:39:48.000
The fire will kill us all!

734
00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:49.400
We're gonna be fine.

735
00:39:49.400 --> 00:39:51.400
Don't worry!

736
00:39:51.400 --> 00:39:53.460
We'll live, somehow.

737
00:39:53.780 --> 00:39:54.850
[NOBLE SOLDIER E]
Hey, are you nuts?

738
00:39:54.850 --> 00:39:56.020
You're going the wrong way!

739
00:39:56.020 --> 00:39:56.790
- [NOBLE SOLDIERS gasp]
- [SABO grunts]

740
00:39:56.790 --> 00:39:58.350
[SABO]
Open the gate, now!

741
00:39:58.350 --> 00:39:59.960
[NOBLE SOLDIER H]
What are you talking about?

742
00:39:59.960 --> 00:40:02.790
[NOBLE SOLDIER H grunting]
Dumb brat!

743
00:40:02.790 --> 00:40:04.400
Go home!

744
00:40:04.400 --> 00:40:05.340
[NOBLE SOLDIER I yelps]

745
00:40:05.340 --> 00:40:08.440
Luffy! Ace! Run!

746
00:40:08.440 --> 00:40:13.120
[SABO groaning]

747
00:40:13.120 --> 00:40:14.430
[NOBLE SOLDIER J]
Let go, brat!

748
00:40:14.430 --> 00:40:15.940
Stay away from the lock!

749
00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:19.380
Open the gate! [groans]

750
00:40:19.380 --> 00:40:20.850
Stop!

751
00:40:20.850 --> 00:40:22.850
No!

752
00:40:22.850 --> 00:40:24.250
[SABO yells]

753
00:40:29.760 --> 00:40:32.160
[NOBLE SOLDIER L]
Why don'tcha be a good
kid and get outta here!

754
00:40:32.160 --> 00:40:33.700
[NOBLE SOLDIER M]
Don't give us any more trouble!

755
00:40:34.160 --> 00:40:37.230
[SABO groaning]

756
00:40:37.230 --> 00:40:40.300
[SABO]
I'm sorry, guys.

757
00:41:02.820 --> 00:41:05.530
[DRAGON]
What happened to you, boy?

758
00:41:05.530 --> 00:41:09.560
[SABO groaning]

759
00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:12.270
[SABO]
Who's there?

760
00:41:15.340 --> 00:41:21.440
[SABO]
Whoever you are, listen, the nobles
are the ones behind this fire.

761
00:41:23.740 --> 00:41:25.770
[SABO]
You gotta believe me!

762
00:41:27.170 --> 00:41:30.340
[SABO]
High Town reeks worse
than Gray Terminal ever did.

763
00:41:30.340 --> 00:41:34.490
The people act civilized, but on
the inside, they're all rotten!

764
00:41:34.490 --> 00:41:38.830
They only care about making themselves
look good, no matter what it takes!

765
00:41:38.830 --> 00:41:40.330
I can't stay here.

766
00:41:40.330 --> 00:41:43.370
If I do, then I'll never be free!

767
00:41:46.340 --> 00:41:48.900
I'm ashamed of being born noble!

768
00:41:48.900 --> 00:41:50.700
I hate myself!

769
00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:56.410
[DRAGON]
Goa Kingdom, look what you've done to this
child, how you've turned him against you.

770
00:41:57.410 --> 00:41:59.840
[DRAGON]
I know how you feel.

771
00:41:59.840 --> 00:42:02.510
I was born in this country, too.

772
00:42:03.850 --> 00:42:08.950
[DRAGON]
But I alone do not have the power to change
this world, and maybe I never will.

773
00:42:08.950 --> 00:42:10.190
But at least...

774
00:42:10.190 --> 00:42:12.860
At least you're actually
listening to me, aren't you?

775
00:42:12.860 --> 00:42:16.200
[DRAGON]
Of course I am, and I'll never forget.
